{"uid":"6991604baea8552b","name":"test_profile_shorthand_header_reaches_status_hub_and_job_yaml_with_no_flag","fullName":"tests.test_llm_header_visibility#test_profile_shorthand_header_reaches_status_hub_and_job_yaml_with_no_flag","historyId":"08c4f6349cb675ef2d02de1dfd208ce0","time":{"start":1791980496857,"stop":1791980498261,"duration":1404},"description":"End to end through the REAL CLI, a real run (task 011, PRD\n    requirement D.2): a profile's own top-level `headers:` shorthand,\n    started with NO `--llm-header` flag on the command line at all, shows\n    its name and value on all THREE surfaces this task's own gate names --\n    `ralphctl --json status`, the hub's `run_detail` payload, and the\n    redacted `ralphctl docs job.yaml` view -- not merely on the reader\n    function task 010's own tests called directly\n    (`read_llm_wiring_headers`).\n\n    Uses the STUB_DOCKER_LIVE_ENGINE knob (same mechanism as\n    `tests/test_cli_start_nodetach.py`/`tests/test_llm_header_e2e.py`) so\n    `status.json` is written by a REAL `ralphd-engine` process reaching a\n    real terminal state, not fabricated by a test helper -- `ralphctl\n    status` genuinely has something on disk (and, before the supervisor's\n    kill, a live API) to read.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>End to end through the REAL CLI, a real run (task 011, PRD<br />\nrequirement D.2): a profile's own top-level <code>headers:</code> shorthand,<br />\nstarted with NO <code>--llm-header</code> flag on the command line at all, shows<br />\nits name and value on all THREE surfaces this task's own gate names --<br />\n<code>ralphctl --json status</code>, the hub's <code>run_detail</code> payload, and the<br />\nredacted <code>ralphctl docs job.yaml</code> view -- not merely on the reader<br />\nfunction task 010's own tests called directly<br />\n(<code>read_llm_wiring_headers</code>).</p>\n<pre><code>Uses the STUB_DOCKER_LIVE_ENGINE knob (same mechanism as\n`tests/test_cli_start_nodetach.py`/`tests/test